            "paragraph": "Figure 1. Neural network development workflow. Blue arrows represent the training steps, while red arrows correspond to the inference process. During training, the \"mapping\" step aggregates aerosol species across modes from the MAM7 output to construct the input XMAM. The MAM7 output is then used to calculate the MAMnet loss (calculated as the minimum mean square difference between the model prediction and the MAM7 fields). During inference, input from MERRA-2 is used to predict the aerosol size distribution and mixing state. MAMnet consists of a single input layer (black), seven hidden layers (orange), and one output layer (green). T and AIRD represent the temperature and air density, respectively. Ns is the number of samples.",
